  "items": [
    {
      "name": "Hammer Barrage",
      "type": "weapon",
      "img": "icons/weapons/hammers/hammer-double-stone-worn.webp",
      "system": {
        "description": {
          "value": "<p>The Hammer Bro's signature attack: a rapid-fire barrage of thrown hammers that arc over obstacles and descend on targets with trajectories calculated through instinct rather than conscious math. Each hammer is a standard construction hammer—metal head, wooden handle, nothing magical about it individually—but the VOLUME and ACCURACY of the throws transforms mundane tools into a devastating ranged attack.</p><p>As an action, a Hammer Bro throws two hammers at targets it can see within 40 feet. Each hammer requires a separate attack roll (+5 to hit) and deals 1d8 + 3 bludgeoning damage on a hit. The hammers arc over half cover and three-quarters cover (though not total cover), reflecting the Hammer Bro's trained ability to throw in parabolic trajectories that bypass obstacles between thrower and target.</p><p>The unlimited supply remains unexplained. After combat, hammers thrown by Hammer Bros are found at impact sites as normal, non-magical hammers. They don't disappear. They don't return. New ones simply appear in the Hammer Bro's hands when needed. Investigation into this phenomenon has been classified as \"not worth the headache\" by the Mages' Guild.</p>",
          "chat": "<p>Hammers arc through the air in quantities that shouldn't be possible, descending on targets with the inevitability of rain and considerably more impact.</p>"
        },
        "unidentified": {
          "name": "Infinite Hammer Throws",
          "description": "<p>This creature throws hammers in rapid succession from an apparently unlimited supply, arcing them over obstacles to reach targets.</p>"
