    {
      "name": "Paired Tactics",
      "type": "feat",
      "img": "icons/skills/melee/weapons-crossed-swords-yellow.webp",
      "system": {
        "description": {
          "value": "<p>Hammer Bros operate in paired teams that coordinate their attacks for maximum effectiveness. When two Hammer Bros are within 15 feet of each other and attacking the same target, both gain advantage on their hammer throw attack rolls as the dual barrage from different angles makes effective dodging nearly impossible. Additionally, when one Hammer Bro of a pair is attacked, the other can use its reaction to throw a hammer at the attacker (+5 to hit, 1d8 + 3 bludgeoning damage), discouraging enemies from engaging either member of the pair individually.</p><p>Breaking a Hammer Bro pair—killing one, separating them, or forcing one to retreat—immediately reduces the survivor's effectiveness and morale. A lone Hammer Bro has disadvantage on attack rolls for 1 round after its partner is eliminated, as the coordination reflexes trained into paired operation produce hesitation when the expected partner isn't there.</p>",
          "chat": "<p>They work in pairs because paired hammers create patterns that single hammers can't. Breaking the pair is priority one. Surviving the pair is priority zero.</p>"
        },
