    {
      "name": "Platform Hopping",
      "type": "feat",
      "img": "icons/skills/movement/arrow-upward-blue.webp",
      "system": {
        "description": {
          "value": "<p>Hammer Bros hop. It's part of their fighting style—a rhythmic bouncing that keeps them in motion, makes them harder to hit, and provides the elevated launch angle that allows their hammer arcs to clear obstacles. The hopping looks ridiculous from a distance and is extremely effective from combat range, as the constant vertical movement complicates targeting for enemies trying to return fire.</p><p>While hopping (which Hammer Bros do automatically during combat), attacks against them have disadvantage if the attacker is at the same elevation or lower. Attacks from above are unaffected—the hopping provides lateral evasion, not overhead protection. The hopping also allows Hammer Bros to move across gaps up to 10 feet wide without requiring ability checks, their rhythmic bouncing carrying them across spaces that would require standard Troopas to find alternate routes.</p>",
          "chat": "<p>Hop. Throw. Hop. Throw. The rhythm is annoying and effective in exactly equal measure.</p>"
        },
